    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_2",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Wire are an English rock band, formed in London in October 1976 by Colin Newman (vocals, guitar), Graham Lewis (bass, vocals), Bruce Gilbert (guitar) and Robert Gotobed (drums). They were originally associated with the punk rock scene, appearing on \"The Roxy London WC2\" album – a key early document of the scene – and were later central to the development of post-punk.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
      "value": 0.8327098427336239,
